# SQLite journals. The catalogs themselves are tracked, but these two are not:
# `-shm` is a shared-memory index meaningless outside the running process, and
# `-wal` is machine-local — a `.db`/`-wal` pair captured at two different
# instants is a corrupt combination. `scripts/checkpoint-sqlite.mjs` folds the
# log back into the `.db` on commit so the tracked file stands alone.
*.db-shm
*.db-wal

# Embody / Envoy (auto-managed)
Backup/
logs/
CrashAutoSave*
.venv/
.mcp.json
opencode.json
.tdn_backup/
